rmatitis and clinical mastitis on the conception rate and calving-conception interval of multiparous and primiparous cows after fixed-time artificial insemination (FTAI) were evaluated. Clinical endometritis was diagnosed by ultrasonography 20-40 days postpartum upon observation of fluid in the uterine lumen. Cows with clinical endometritis were treated intramuscularly with 2 mg/kg...\n\nAuthor(s): Thaisa Campos Marques, Karen Martins Leão, Moraima Castro Rodrigues, Natalia do Carmo Silva and Rossane Pereira da Silva\n\n  * https://doi.org/10.5897/AJB2015.14592\n  * Article Number: 9E9EE1E54154\n\nAbstract--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRecent Developments of New DNA Origami Nanostructures for Drug Delivery (https://openalex.org/W2253670310)\nciteturn139search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11.3 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; DOI: 10.2174/1381612821666150531165551\n# Recent Developments of New DNA Origami Nanostructures for Drug Delivery\n\nOpenAlex ID: W2253670310\n\nDOI: 10.2174/1381612821666150531165551\n\nPMID: 26027568\n\nType: review\n\nYear: 2015\n\nPublication date: 2015-07-13\n\nLanguage: en\n\n## Source\n\nName: Current Pharmaceutical Design\n\nISSN-L: 1381-6128\n\nISSN: 1381-6128, 1873-4286\n\nPublisher: Bentham Science Publishers\n\n## Citation\n\nVolume: 21\n\nIssue: 22\n\nPages: 3181–3190\n\n## Article links\n\n  * Article website\n  * Location website\n\n## Authors\n\n  * Juan Yan (ORCID)\n  * Chongya Hu\n  * Xunwei Liu (ORCID)\n  * Jian Zhong (ORCID)\n  * Gang Sun (ORCID) — Jinan Military General Hospital (ROR)\n  * Dannong He (ORCID) — Shanghai Jiao Tong University (ROR)\n\n## Abstract\n\nDNA origami technique was first introduced in 2006 by Rothemund, it has gained widespread research interest and led to explosive achievements, in which long single-stranded DNA (ssDNA) is folded into a designed nanostructure, in either two dimensions (2D) or three dimensions (3D), with the aid of many shorter staple strands. A series of methods for new design principles for DNA origami nanostructures have already been proposed, ranging from the preparation of scaffold to the folding mechanisms. After that, novel strategies in functionalizing DNA origami nanostructures and their practical applications are gradually becoming research hotspots. This review focuses on the development in the new scaffold design approaches, folding conditions, various nano objects functionalized on DNA origami nanostructures, and their applications as drug carriers in the recent five years. We anticipate more exploratory and extendible work developed based on the summary of progress obtained previously.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAfrican Journal of Biotechnology - Article Cited by (https://academicjournals.org/journal/AJB/cited-by-article/381C21354153)\nciteturn139search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11.3 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago;   * https://doi.org/10.5897/AJB2015.14697\n\n  * Twum Anthony\n  * Department of Physics, University of Cape Coast, Cape Coast, Ghana.\n  * Search for this author on:\n  * Google Scholar\n\n##### Sam Frederick\n\n  * Sam Frederick\n  * Department of Physics, University of Cape Coast, Cape Coast, Ghana.\n  * Search for this author on:\n  * Google Scholar\n\n  * Article Number - 381C21354153\n  * Vol.14(28), pp. 2258-2264 , July 2015\n  * https://doi.org/10.5897/AJB2015.14697\n\n  *  Received: 04 May 2015\n  *  Accepted: 06 July 2015\n  *  Published: 15 July 2015\n\n  * Copyright © 2026 Author(s) retain the copyright of this article.\nThis article is published under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License 4.0.\n\n  * Abstract\n  * Full-Text (PDF)\n  * References\n  * Citations\n  * Authors\n  * Article Metrics\n\nCrossRef Citations (2)\n\nSee more citations on Google Scholar\n\n1.\n\nCrop Improvement\n\n2.\n\nHerms Alexander,Günther Katrin,Sperling Evgeni,Heerwig Andreas,Kick Alfred,Cichos Fran